N:game-ui-ux
D:Design and review the canonical generic game UI/UX contract for HUDs, menus, overlays, screen flow, information hierarchy, input and focus, safe areas, responsive layout, scalable text, localization, accessibility, data binding, and cross-device verification. Validate game-ui-contract.json and route visual concepts or engine widgets outward.
G:game-ui-ux game-ui-design HUD menu inventory shop map settings overlay controller-navigation focus safe-area responsive-game-ui scalable-text localization accessibility state-binding Three.js

U[8]:
  Design or review HUD menu inventory shop map settings tutorial notification and overlay systems
  Map player decisions to information priority persistence context and conflict rules
  Define screen stack modal pause back cancel resume loading error and reconnect behavior
  Support mouse keyboard controller touch and assistive input with predictable focus
  Plan safe areas aspect families responsive constraints text scaling and content reflow
  Treat localization glyphs expansion bidirectional text and input prompts as layout states
  Define event-driven UI data sources stale states errors permissions and hidden-data boundaries
  Verify real interaction across build device viewport input locale and accessibility settings

S[8]{n,step,details}:
  1,Inventory reality,Inspect runtime screens states designs devices locales controller maps and accessibility settings; mockups are partial evidence
  2,Map decisions,Name the player decision status or feedback each element supports and classify urgency persistence visibility and conflict priority
  3,Model flow,Define screens overlays modals push replace pop back resume disconnect destructive actions initial focus traversal and device switching
  4,Define layout,Use constraints containers anchors and content rules; record aspect families safe areas scaling reflow and scroll ownership from target evidence
  5,Define localization,Externalize strings and cover expansion plural formats bidirectional text fonts glyphs line breaks and input-glyph substitution
  6,Define data,Record source event/query initial snapshot update stale permission error and owner; never bind hidden multiplayer data to unauthorized UI
  7,Verify interaction,Test all required states inputs focus back aspects orientation safe areas text scale locales loading errors reduced motion and rapid updates
  8,Validate and route,Run validate-game-ui.py; route visual concepts project-specific Open Design Three.js DOM/canvas engine widgets feel and accessibility outward

R[9]:
  This is the canonical generic lane for game-ui-design game-ui-ux and Three.js game UI planning
  A mockup never deletes runtime states information identity or interactions it omits
  Every element supports a player decision status feedback or legal requirement
  Focus is visible predictable recoverable and able to leave every focusable element
  No universal reference resolution touch size margin or text size replaces target-device evidence
  Critical state never relies on one color audio motion haptic or position channel
  Localization and text scaling are first-class layout states
  Gameplay truth hidden information and presentation state remain separate
  Static screenshots do not prove navigation state updates or accessibility

